Quest segment A rehearsal on the 2026-11-11 06:45 build, 06:58-07:40
Probe DLL APBQuestProbe.dll SHA-256 580C457384A54B23811761F44FF0C8BBE0C17F7188AE5133AA126067B10D0407 (release DLL 01d4e1ed and trace DLL aba1d4f6 of the same build)
Command: build/catchup/run-quest-series.ps1 -Prefix qs-c -Order off,acc,skip,skip,acc,off -Trials 1
Profile APB-CatchUp-Test, FramerateLimit 30, game window in front 100% in all six launches, dropped rows 0.
"acc" = accelerate with the release read rule; "skip" = the same plus the test rule SetSkipBlocked (APB_CATCHUP_SKIP=1); "off" = same mod list, VM catch-up not installed.

What was new in this build for the probe: the gate's menu part is the release plugin's code (src/MenuWatch.h): the loading and main
menus by their own events, one reading of the UI at kPostLoadGame, the pause read when the gate is asked. HUD-type menu events no
longer close the gate (probes up to the 19:08 build closed it on every menu event). First quest run of the fixed skip rule (order
restore of the 20:58 / 22:46 builds) and of the gate_closes counter.

RESULT
- All six trials ended normally and identically: stage order 20 30 40 48 50 60, stage 48 after the graph event (66-68 ms), scene
  phases 0..29, 24 Esbern/Delphine lines (digest fdb15642cc), end state digest 995561791e, reload equal, no end-state line differing
  from the first off trial. guard_violations 0.
- acc: 2,324 / 2,269 extra cycles, 5,066 / 4,867 extra calls. skip: 4,649 / 4,777 cycles, 10,388 / 10,737 extra calls,
  16,411 / 16,963 front skips, the queue rebuilt after 4 / 5 cycles (first time the rebuild ran inside a quest trial).
- The gate: after each of the twelve loading screens of the four catch-up trials (start-save travel, inn door, end reload) counted
  frames resumed within 3 s of the Loading Menu close event (87-124 frames in those 3 s; 40 after one end reload). So the gate was
  never left closed, neither by a close event nor by the reading at kPostLoadGame.
- gate_closes = 0 in every trial although each has three loading screens and a save load (gameplayReady goes false at
  kPreLoadGame). The counter only counts a VM update that finds the gate closed, so no VM update reached the hook while a load was
  in progress. It therefore says nothing about loads; a 0 here does show that none of the 65 HUD-type menu events of a trial
  (71 menu events in qs-c-02-acc) closed the gate under a running VM.
- Whether the old gate cost anything in this segment cannot be shown from these runs: against the 19:08 probe (qs-b-02/05-acc,
  qs-b-03/04-skip) counted frames per second of scene (27.5-28.0) and cycles per frame (acc 0.355-0.364, skip 0.673-0.714) are
  the same within the spread between trials. If every one of ~65 events had cost two frames, that would be about 2% of the frames.
- Loading hang: none. Segment A totals are now 30 trials: catch-up on 14 with 1 hang (qs-a-02-skip, cause open), off 16 with 0.
- Every launch left two crash logs after the window was closed (execute access violation at 0x7FF5DF460000 / 0x7FF5DF450000, also in
  the two off launches where VM catch-up is not installed). In one of the twelve (qs-c-04-skip, 07:25:17) the stack scan lists an
  address of this project for the first time: APBQuestProbe.dll+003E08C at RSP+0x40, the instruction after the hook's call of the
  engine's AttemptFunctionCall (VMCatchUp.cpp:645, TaskletCall). It is not a live return address of the faulting chain: the fault's
  return address is at RSP+0 (SkyrimUpscaler.dll+02C3807), the next code address is RicochetFramework's input hook at RSP+0x30
  (its epilogue restores xmm6 from [rsp+0x20], so its frame is at least 0x30 bytes), and RSP+0x40 lies inside that frame. The
  crash thread is a job thread, which also runs tasklets, so the value is what an earlier tasklet call left on that stack. The
  chain that faulted is input hook -> SkyrimUpscaler -> freed address, as in the earlier exit crashes.

NOT COVERED: the release DLL itself, a pausing menu or a dialogue menu during play (segment A opens none), 42 FPS, the
catchup-skipfront comparison on this build. This is a rehearsal of one trial per launch, not the main run.

